# arm64 + wasm excluded: this property test surfaced a SECOND, distinct
# two-word-string bug (independent of the string_from_bytes fix — it
# fails on wasm too, which has no freelist). A `string[]` built by
# appending freshly-sliced two-word strings *inside a loop* and returned
# from a function corrupts the earlier elements' bytes. A loop appending
# a string *literal* works; the same appends *unrolled* work; only the
# loop+slice combination on two-word backends (arm64, wasm) fails.
# Single-word backends (interp, x86_64) are correct. Tracked in
# docs/FEATURE-AUDIT.md; re-add arm64/wasm here once fixed.
interp x86_64
